messages:
nina: FYI i'm opening a PR to update the pricing page examples and to clarify rate-limit headers across SDKs. goal: one canonical curl + python + node sample that uses the new X-Usage-Tier header and shows how 429s are returned when quota exhausted.

omar: nice. can you show the exact 429 response example? customers get confused whether 429 means billing blocked or temporary throttle.

nina: plan: show 429 body `{"error":"quota_exceeded", "retry_after": 30}` and note that retry_after is in seconds and that requests in grace window still return 200 but are billed.

jia: also please add a very short line about headers precedence: `X-Usage-Tier` overrides account default tier for request-level billing attribution. that helped a customer today.

nina: added that. branch: https://github.com/redwood/docs/pull/5999 (pricing-header-samples)

docs-ci-bot: running linter and snippet-tests on PR #5999.

omar: one nit: in the node snippet show `headers` as an explicit field to avoid confusion with env-level API key usage.

nina: updated node snippet accordingly. node example now: ````
// node (SDKv3)
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const resp = await client.generate({
  model: 'open-7b',
  input: 'Explain rate limits concisely',
  headers: { 'X-Usage-Tier': 'pro' }
});
````

jia: LGTM. two checklist items before merge: 1) add cross-ref from rate-limits guide to this pricing example, 2) ensure snippet-tests assert header presence in recorded HTTP fixtures.

docs-ci-bot: snippet-tests passed, lint passed. all green at 3305556702.

nina: merged and will post a short note in #docs once site rebuild completes. thanks!
